  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "How many of these fractions are in least terms?\n$$\\frac{1}{2000},\\frac{2}{2000},\\frac{3}{2000},\\ldots,\\frac{1999}{2000}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$800$",
      "worked": "A fraction $\\frac{a}{2000}$ is in least terms exactly when $a$ and $2000$ are coprime. Since $2000$ itself is not coprime to $2000$, the required count is $\\phi(2000)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2000&=2^4\\times5^3,\\\\\\phi(2000)&=\\phi(2^4)\\phi(5^3),\\\\\\phi(2000)&=(2^4-2^3)(5^3-5^2),\\\\\\phi(2000)&=8\\times100,\\\\\\phi(2000)&=800.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $800$ fractions are in least terms.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
